<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::offensive_strike_rate" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::chip_prod_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in offensive strikes targeting shipping, ports, and regional infrastructure in the Gulf rapidly disrupts logistics and energy supplies (and damages intermediate suppliers), causing semiconductor fabs and their supply chains to miss inputs or shipments and reducing effective production throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::offensive_strike_rate" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A higher tempo of offensive strikes in the theater increases the number of direct attacks on commercial vessels, mines laid, and near-miss incidents as combatants and proxies target or mistake shipping, raising maritime security incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
