<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::retaliatory_strike_rate" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharper tempo of retaliatory strikes raises regional and global risk premia and sanctions‑compliance concerns, prompting institutional investors and banks to pull back or delay funding for geopolitically exposed AI projects and reducing near‑term capital flows into the AI sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::retaliatory_strike_rate" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::seaborne_hydrocarb_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An increased rate of retaliatory strikes raising the likelihood of hits on export terminals, loading infrastructure, or tankers directly reduces export operations and forces cancellations or suspensions of seaborne hydrocarbon shipments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::retaliatory_strike_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_attack_intensit" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in Iran's retaliatory-strike tempo signals/reflects increased operational activity and willingness to employ or export munitions and tactical systems (e.g., armed UAVs, missiles) that Iran can transfer to Russia, enabling Moscow to increase strike rates in Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
