  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp escalations and visible use of commercially sourced dual‑use technologies (drones, comms, EW) prompt rapid policy responses (export controls, investment screening) and political pressure to harderen tech decoupling between the US and strategic competitors, raising geopolitical technology tension.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_attack_intensit" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher rates of offensive strikes (missiles, drones, naval gunfire) near coastlines and ports directly increase the number and severity of attacks, near-misses and damage events affecting ships and sea lanes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_attack_intensit" target="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Sudden increases in strike intensity produce acute geopolitical uncertainty and rapid portfolio reallocation (flight-to-safety, stop-losses, hedging) that raises realized volatility in global sovereign bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
