<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::chokepoint_transit_capac" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::chip_prod_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions in physical transit capacity through key chokepoints delay or block delivery of critical semiconductor inputs and heavy fab equipment, forcing fabs to slow or suspend production and lowering effective chip production throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::chokepoint_transit_capac" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical reductions or closures of key straits (e.g., minefields, port closures, or convoy restrictions) directly limit the number of tankers and LNG carriers that can transit, immediately lowering seaborne energy export volumes from Black Sea/adjacent Russian terminals.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
