  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in seaborne hydrocarbon flows eases energy supply pressures and inflation expectations and reduces term premia, thereby lowering long-dated sovereign bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
