<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::geo_tech_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp uptick in hostile or disruptive maritime incidents (attacks, seizures) immediately triggers defensive policy responses (sanctions, export controls, reciprocal tech restrictions) and accelerated decoupling steps that raise geopolitical technology tension between China and the US.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" target="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in maritime security incidents create sudden supply and geopolitical uncertainty that trigger rapid portfolio reallocation and flight-to-quality moves, producing sharp, immediate increases in realized volatility in sovereign bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" target="global_monetary_stress::fx_intervention_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher frequency/severity of incidents disrupts export receipts and amplifies exchange-rate swings for exposed currencies, prompting authorities to step into FX markets with purchases or sales to smooth volatility and defend exchange-rate targets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" target="russia_ukraine_war::trade_and_transport_rest" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Attacks, seizures, or mine incidents on commercial vessels provoke coastal states, ports, and insurers to impose routing bans, naval escorts, and formal/informal port restrictions, thereby increasing trade and transport constraints for goods tied to the conflict zone.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::maritime_security_incide" target="russia_ukraine_war::regional_spillover_incid" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Hostile or accidental maritime incidents in or near contested waters increase the likelihood of cross-border naval engagements, interdictions, or diplomatic/military responses by neighboring states, raising the rate of regional spillover incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
