<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::market_risk_perception" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated market perception of maritime supply‑chain risk raises investor risk premia and prompts lenders and VCs to pull back financing for capital‑intensive AI infrastructure and projects—especially those sited in or dependent on exposed trade corridors—reducing capital flows to AI.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::market_risk_perception" target="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in market risk perception raises risk premia and accelerates forced and discretionary portfolio rebalancing, directly increasing intraday and realized volatility in bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_maritime_chokepoi::market_risk_perception" target="us_iran_confrontation::strike_auth_propensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in market-perceived risk and energy-price volatility create political and economic pressure on US decision‑makers to authorize offensive actions aimed at securing supply routes or deterring further disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
