<edge source="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in bond-market volatility increase market-wide risk aversion and trigger redemptions and value-at-risk driven de-risking by funds, reducing new equity and debt allocations into AI projects and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">china_us_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::market_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in bond-market volatility drive broad investor risk aversion and repricing, directly raising market participants' perception of geopolitical and supply-disruption risk that is applied to maritime energy exposure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_export_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp spikes in bond-market volatility tighten trade finance and commodity lending lines and push up insurance and margin requirements for energy shipments, producing delays, cancellations or reduced volumes of cross-border energy exports from Russia and Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::bond_market_volatility" target="us_iran_confrontation::military_presence_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute bond-market volatility produces risk-off shocks that threaten energy and shipping markets and investor confidence, prompting the US to surge naval and air assets to the Gulf and nearby sea lanes to deter disruptions and reassure markets and partners.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
