<edge source="global_monetary_stress::bilateral_exchange_rate" target="china_us_tech_rivalry::chip_prod_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A significant depreciation of a major chip-producing country's currency versus currencies used to invoice fab equipment and imported materials raises local costs for capacity expansion, delaying or shrinking planned production ramp-ups.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
